-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1107: a WITHIN written as a name or an expression. Each
-- rule is `literal` with its deadline spelt another way, so `l4 explore` and
-- `l4 lts` on it should say what they say of `literal`. `raises` is a name
-- whose working out divides by zero: neither tool may crash on it, and its
-- deadline is not known.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF Alice
DECLARE Act IS ONE OF pay

`ten days` MEANS 10
`five and five` MEANS 5 PLUS 5
`no period` MEANS 10 DIVIDED BY 0

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`literal` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN 10 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`named` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `ten days` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`sum` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN 5 PLUS 5 LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`named sum` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `five and five` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Act
`raises` MEANS PARTY Alice MUST pay WITHIN `no period` LEST BREACH BY Alice BECAUSE "late"
